--- DEMO 5: Spectral Gap Theorem (Exact) ---

  n=3: gap = 4/3 = 1.333333, mixing = 3/4 = 0.75 flips, T(n) = ? classes
  n=4: gap = 4/6 = 0.666667, mixing = 6/4 = 1.50 flips, T(n) = ? classes
  n=5: gap = 4/10 = 0.400000, mixing = 10/4 = 2.50 flips, T(n) = ? classes
  n=6: gap = 4/15 = 0.266667, mixing = 15/4 = 3.75 flips, T(n) = ? classes
  n=7: gap = 4/21 = 0.190476, mixing = 21/4 = 5.25 flips, T(n) = ? classes
  n=8: gap = 4/28 = 0.142857, mixing = 28/4 = 7.00 flips, T(n) = ? classes


--- DEMO 6: Heat Kernel as Polynomial ---

  P(u) = sum_k m_k * u^k  where u = q^(1/10):
    u^-10  coefficient = 1
    u^ -5  coefficient = 1
    u^ +5  coefficient = 3

  This polynomial EXACTLY encodes the heat kernel.
  K(ln(q)) = P(q^(1/10)) for any algebraic q > 0.
  No exp(), no ln(), no transcendental functions.
  Just polynomial evaluation in one algebraic number.

